From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] usb: cdns3: sky1: activate wrapper before children to fix
 runtime-PM order

On O6N (CIX Sky1) each USB controller is described in ACPI as a
cdnsp-sky1 wrapper (CIXH2030:0N) with a nested cdns,usbssp child
(CIXH2031:0N). The child's own probe (cdns3-plat) calls
pm_runtime_set_active() + pm_runtime_enable() on itself, which requires
its parent to already be runtime-PM active.

cdnsp_sky1_probe() only marked the wrapper runtime-active at the very end
of probe, *after* populating the children:

	if (!ACPI_COMPANION(dev)) of_platform_populate(...);   /* binds kids */
	else /* set child platform_data; ACPI binds kids async */
	device_set_wakeup_capable(dev, true);
	pm_runtime_set_active(dev);
	pm_runtime_enable(dev);

So when a child activated while the wrapper was runtime-PM-enabled but not
yet RPM_ACTIVE, the PM core emitted, per controller:

  runtime PM trying to activate child device CIXH2031:0N but parent
    (CIXH2030:0N) is not active
  Enabling runtime PM for inactive device with active children

~19 lines of benign but noisy output across the ten Sky1 USB instances.

Root cause is init ordering: the child uses runtime PM before the parent
wrapper is runtime-active. Fix it by marking the wrapper active first --
move device_set_wakeup_capable()/pm_runtime_set_active()/
pm_runtime_enable() ahead of child population so the parent is RPM_ACTIVE
before any child binds (the DT populate that follows binds children
synchronously; under ACPI they are enumerated asynchronously).

The wrapper is a pure clock/reset/register glue whose runtime
suspend/resume callbacks are no-ops, so it never needs to gate on child
activity for its own runtime PM. Mark it pm_suspend_ignore_children() as
well: this both silences the two warnings deterministically and closes the
asynchronous ACPI probe-order window that reordering alone cannot cover.
Error paths after the (now earlier) pm_runtime_enable() unwind runtime PM
via a new err_pm label.

No functional change to USB enumeration or system suspend/resume; only the
spurious runtime-PM boot warnings are removed.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/cdns3/cdnsp-sky1.c
@@ -762,12 +762,37 @@
 			}
 		}
 	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Mark the wrapper (CIXH2030) runtime-active and enable runtime PM
+	 * *before* the child controllers (CIXH2031/cdns,usbssp) are populated
+	 * and bound.  Each child calls pm_runtime_set_active() in its own
+	 * probe; if the parent wrapper is already runtime-PM-enabled but not
+	 * yet RPM_ACTIVE at that moment, the PM core logs, per child,
+	 *   "runtime PM trying to activate child device CIXH2031:0N but parent
+	 *    (CIXH2030:0N) is not active"
+	 * and, on the wrapper itself,
+	 *   "Enabling runtime PM for inactive device with active children".
+	 * The DT populate below binds children synchronously, and under ACPI
+	 * the children are enumerated asynchronously, so activating the parent
+	 * first makes the child activation legal in both cases.
+	 *
+	 * pm_suspend_ignore_children() additionally decouples this always-on
+	 * register/clock glue -- whose runtime suspend/resume are no-ops --
+	 * from the children's runtime-PM accounting, which also closes the
+	 * asynchronous ACPI probe-order window.
+	 */
+	device_set_wakeup_capable(dev, true);
+	pm_runtime_set_active(dev);
+	pm_suspend_ignore_children(dev, true);
+	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
+
 	if (!ACPI_COMPANION(dev)) {
 		cdns_sky1_auxdata->platform_data = cdns_sky1_pdata;
 		ret = of_platform_populate(node, NULL, cdns_sky1_auxdata, dev);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(dev, "failed to create children: %d\n", ret);
-			goto err;
+			goto err_pm;
 		}
 	} else {
 		/*
@@ -791,15 +816,14 @@
 			if (id && !cdev->platform_data)
 				cdev->platform_data = cdns_sky1_pdata;
 			else
-				goto err;
+				goto err_pm;
 		}
 	}

-	device_set_wakeup_capable(dev, true);
-	pm_runtime_set_active(dev);
-	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
 	return 0;
-err:
+err_pm:
+	pm_runtime_disable(dev);
+	pm_runtime_set_suspended(dev);
 	kfree(cdns_sky1_pdata);
 	return ret;
 }
